{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1235286-concealed-weapons","id":1235286,"title":"Concealed Weapons.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-15T10:19:39-07:00","id":1235286,"title":"Concealed Weapons.","content":"Any advise on how Penguns or Sword Canes work mechanicly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T16:20:20-07:00","id":1238087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1235286-concealed-weapons#post1235286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advise on how Penguns or Sword Canes work mechanicly?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to draw the weapon before using it, just like you'd have to draw a sword from its sheath or a knife from wherever you're concealing it. Are you asking for what it would take for some other character to notice it for what it is, rather than the mundane object it looks like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T05:36:42-07:00","id":1238186,"title":"","content":"basicly yes.<br /> <br /> What equipment rating should it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T09:25:54-07:00","id":1238253,"title":"","content":"Probably weakest in category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:28:11-07:00","id":1238296,"title":"","content":"They are effectively derringers, usually in .22 caliber or 9mm. 3 or 4 damage IIRC, with only a single shot. Pen guns can be concealed in a pocket; cane guns can't. Carrying one is, legally, the same as carrying a concealed firearm, as far as I'm aware. Guide to the Technocracy gave pen guns a device cost of 4, but I consider that rather high. 2 is probably more reasonable, given that there are companies that sell them on the open market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T18:38:45-07:00","id":1238457,"title":"","content":"A sword or gun in a cane is definitely a &quot;concealed&quot; weapon, but in my opinion, since the cane acts more like camouflage, I'd assign a difficulty for perception checks to see what it really is, rather than a size-based concealment category. Something as small as a pen gun could be concealed in your pocket, and it might still take a perception check to see through the camouflage when you pull it out.<br /> <br /> Here are a couple of interesting examples I found on Youtube...<br /> Pen gun from the 1990s: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HhnpKyORQy8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HhnpKyORQy8</a><br /> Cane guns from the 1850s-1870s: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N0CLhZMA_Rk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N0CLhZMA_Rk</a><br /> Interesting antique canes, including a cane sword: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=glC9uK1wirk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=glC9uK1wirk</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}